   "source": [
    "### Section 3: Reporting Integrity Index\n",
    "**Failure Modes in Logistics Reporting**\n",
    "\n",
    "In cold chain environments, incident reporting can fail through:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Underreporting (drivers avoid logging excursions)\n",
    "\n",
    "* Delayed logging (entered days later)\n",
    "\n",
    "* Severity downgrading\n",
    "\n",
    "* “Resolved in transit” narratives\n",
    "\n",
    "* Site-level KPI gaming\n",
    "\n",
    "If reporting integrity is degraded, the EWI can indicate false improvement.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c514ff12",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.007079,
     "end_time": "2026-02-18T08:50:04.409406",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2026-02-18T08:50:04.402327",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "**Reporting Friction Metrics**\n",
    "We must therefore also track:\n",
    "\n",
    "• Time from event_date → capa_open_date\n",
    "\n",
    "• % of events opened same day\n",
    "\n",
    "• % of “Minor” events with long excursion minutes\n",
    "\n",
    "• Detection channel distribution shifts\n",
    "\n",
    "• Sudden drop in event volume\n",
    "\n",
    "Silence, in these circumstances, does not equal success."
   ]
  },
