   "source": [
    "Operational KPIs are only as reliable as reporting discipline. Real-time logging is foundational to accurate risk detection. A decline in event volume or increase in reporting delay should be treated as a governance signal, not an operational improvement."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "94763bcc",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.013726,
     "end_time": "2026-02-18T08:50:06.536769",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2026-02-18T08:50:06.523043",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "The structure within the reporting system itself might be causing latency.  Process centralization might result in batch submission, causing a delay in the start of the \"CAPA clock.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "096db08b",
   "metadata": {
    "papermill": {
     "duration": 0.013567,
     "end_time": "2026-02-18T08:50:06.564415",
     "exception": false,
     "start_time": "2026-02-18T08:50:06.550848",
     "status": "completed"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "In centralized reporting environments, formal CAPA timestamps may reflect administrative workflow rather than operational detection timing. This can create the appearance of strong closure performance while masking real-time visibility gaps."
   ]
  }
